                <pb facs="0247" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 165.</note>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 143.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 29, 1870</date>. (Received October
                    14.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In pursuance of your instruction of August
                    30 (No. 128) I addressed to the secretary for foreign affairs a request that
                    measures might be taken for the protection of the large amount of American
                    property in Paris upon its occupation by the German troops.</p>
                <p>I append a translation of the reply of Mr. von Thiele conveying the desired
                    assurances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d165-a1.xml" xpointer="d165-a1"/>
